{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/pulls/1","id":4867392405,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVKRIlc8AAAABIh6DlQ","html_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/issues/1","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Close registered channels when event loop shutdown starts after the pre-task check","user":{"login":"codexcoder21","id":216437543,"node_id":"U_kgDODOaTJw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216437543?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21","html_url":"https://github.com/codexcoder21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\n\nThe UrlProtocol test `testProtocolRootCloseCallerRacingEventLoopShutdown` (added by https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/605) fails intermittently in CI with `Iteration 40: the root is closed` — every close caller's promise had completed and the event loop had terminated, but the channel was still open (for example https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/actions/runs/38663196732/job/116189023105, 2397 of 2398 tests passed). That failure is blocking https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/702, a reviewed fix the organization needs to land, and the defect behind it is in Netty's event-loop shutdown path rather than in UrlProtocol.\n\n## The defect\n\n`SingleThreadIoEventLoop.run()` only called `ioHandler.prepareToDestroy()` — the step that closes every channel still registered with the loop — when it saw `isShuttingDown()` at one point in each iteration, *before* `runAllTasks(...)`. If shutdown is requested after that check (from a task running on the loop, from a close listener, or from another thread during that window), the loop runs its tasks, `confirmShutdown()` returns `true` (immediately, with a zero quiet period), `run()` exits, and `SingleThreadEventExecutor.doStartThread` goes straight through its final drains to `cleanup()`. For NIO, `NioIoHandler.destroy()` only closes the selector, so a registered channel is left open and still reported as registered, with its `closeFuture()` never completing. Any later `channel.close()` from another thread is rejected (`RejectedExecutionException: event executor terminated` from `AbstractChannelHandlerContext.safeExecute`), so its promise fails while the channel stays open.\n\nReproduction (public API, deterministic): register a `NioSocketChannel` on a one-thread `MultiThreadIoEventLoopGroup`, call `group.shutdownGracefully(0, 5, SECONDS)` from a task submitted to that loop, await termination: the channel is still open. Before this change that happens every time.\n\n## The change\n\n- `SingleThreadIoEventLoop` now overrides `confirmShutdown()`: when the loop is shutting down it calls `ioHandler.prepareToDestroy()` and then `super.confirmShutdown()`. Every shutdown confirmation — the one at the end of each `run()` iteration and the executor's own final task and shutdown-hook drains in `doStartThread` — therefore closes the loop's registrations before the loop can terminate, regardless of when shutdown was requested. The old check before `runAllTasks(...)` is removed because it is now subsumed. `IoHandler.prepareToDestroy()` is documented as callable multiple times, and the previous code already called it on every iteration while shutting down. This is the same ordering `ManualIoEventLoop` already uses (`handler.prepareToDestroy()` immediately before its `confirmShutdown()`).\n- Three tests in `NioEventLoopTest`, each failing before the change:\n  - `testShutdownFromTaskClosesRegisteredChannel` — shutdown started from a task on the loop.\n  - `testShutdownFromCloseListenerClosesOtherChannel` — shutdown started from a close listener on one channel must still close a second registered channel.\n  - `testShutdownHookRegistrationClosesChannel` — a channel registered by a shutdown hook (run during the executor's final drains) is also closed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Fail-first: with only `SingleThreadIoEventLoop.java` reverted to `4.2` (`aa00c11`), `./mvnw -pl transport -am -Dtest=NioEventLoopTest#<the three new tests> test` gives **Tests run: 3, Failures: 3, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0** — each fails on `channel.isOpen()` after `terminationFuture()` completed (`expected: <false> but was: <true>`, `NioEventLoopTest.java:88`, `:108`, `:129`).\n- With the change, the whole `netty-transport` module test suite (`./mvnw -pl transport test`, JDK 21): **Tests run: 422, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 9** (all 9 skips are in untouched test classes with existing `@Disabled` tests: `LocalTransportThreadModelTest3`, `LocalTransportThreadModelTest`, `SingleThreadIoEventLoopTest`, `ThreadPerChannelEventLoopGroupTest`). `NioEventLoopTest` 16/16, `SingleThreadEventLoopTest` 18/18, `SingleThreadIoEventLoopTest` 5 run / 1 existing skip.\n- The native transports (epoll, kqueue, io_uring) share `SingleThreadIoEventLoop`; their module tests were not run here.\n- Consumer check (earlier, by the lane that wrote the fix): with jars built from this branch, the UrlProtocol original racing test passed 10/10 and its deterministic reproducer 10/10; on Netty 4.2.10.Final the deterministic reproducer fails 10/10.\n\nThis PR does not publish anything; a fixed Netty build will be published separately and pinned in UrlProtocol, where the deterministic reproducer `tests/testProtocolRootCloseAfterShutdownStartedInEventLoopClosesRoot.kts` is waiting on branch https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/tree/fix/lane137-root-close-pin.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:38:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T02:38:43Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"65fb81c67e3ba92cdf52387bd5cd17cb0f546893","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty-2/statuses/d7b4547b64859311b9317a966cb995385399b8c5","head":{"label":"CodexCoder21Organization:fix/lane132-shutdown-from-task-closes-channels","ref":"fix/lane132-shutdown-from-task-closes-channels","sha":"d7b4547b64859311b9317a966cb995385399b8c5","user":{"login":"CodexCoder21Organization","id":227065596,"node_id":"O_kgDODYi-_A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227065596?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodexCoder21Organization","html_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodexCoder21Organization/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodexCoder21Organization/following{/other